{{Documentation/Header}}
Outputs a literal ampersand (<code>&amp;</code>). Use it inside template parameters and URLs where a bare <code>&amp;</code> would otherwise be read as the start of an HTML entity, or would break parameter parsing.

Takes no parameters.

==Syntax==
{{T|&}}

==Example==
<pre>{{fullurl:Special:Block|wpTarget=Bot{{&}}wpExpiry=indefinite}}</pre>

==See also==
* {{T|Nbsp}} — non-breaking space